-- leading.talk: the canonical-source-leading-group case (spec chapter 11,
-- The canonical source of a Text Pattern). A spliced pattern is a nested
-- group, so splicing one first makes a pattern whose first element is a
-- group, and its canonical source is written `< <`, never `<<`.

script variable unit = <4 digits>
script variable first = nothing
script variable only = nothing
script variable same = nothing

on go
  put <(unit), "x"> into first
  put <(unit)> into only
  put first = < <4 digits>, "x"> into same                    -- true
end go
